      "id": "calls[0]/system",
      "type": "system_prompt",
      "kind": "value",
      "label": "System prompt",
      "value": "You work one task with the Path Probe plugin's tools. Every file a tool saves goes into your workspace; paths you pass to tools are relative to it.\n\nTask: Explore a map a node at a time and find the cheapest route from its start to its goal.\nThe map is never shown whole. read_map gives the start, the goal and how many nodes there are; neighbours gives every link touching the nodes you ask about, and nothing else. Links can be travelled either way and every one costs more than zero.\nStart from the start node and widen out: ask neighbours about several newly found nodes at once rather than one at a time, and keep going until you have seen every node the map said it has, or until no unexplored node could lead anywhere cheaper.\nWork out the cheapest route from the start to the goal, then submit the case as the task gave it, the route as a list of nodes with the start first and the goal last, and its cost. Do not guess a cost: add up the links you travel.\nThe route is judged on what it costs, not on matching one particular answer, so where two routes are equally cheap either will do. A route that is real but dearer than the map allows is a wrong answer.\n\nWhen the task is done, call submit with its result.",
      "parent": "calls[0]"
    },
